# fixedbugs, defect 538, lane b17-emit, 2026-10-09 (panel 200's R1).
#
# Two groups whose headers each compile alone and each declare `twice` of
# another type, so one unit holding both cannot compile. Until 2026-10-09
# this was told as the second header's own refusal, *`fixedbugs-538-int.h`,
# the header this group names, does not compile*, and with the groups swapped
# the other header was blamed (the case beside this one). Both headers are
# told now, on the group whose header sorts first, the same words in both
# orders.

extern "fixedbugs-538-long.h"
    function twice(x: i64) -> i64

extern "fixedbugs-538-int.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function thrice(x: i32) -> i32

function main()
    print(twice(x: 3))
    print(thrice(x: 4))
